{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-11",
  "title": "Co-creative dynamics",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Co-creative dynamics"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "When a client is deeply involved—bringing their technical expertise, collaborative energy, and input—they’re not just paying for a service. they’re becoming a co-creator, which means the dynamic shifts significantly. this kind of engagement demands more from both sides, and it should be reflected in the workflow *and* the pricing."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**why this matters**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **higher intensity collaboration**: involved clients require more real-time communication, adjustments, and flexibility. they’re not just dropping tasks into a black box—they’re co-navigating the process with you."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **dual expertise dynamic**: their curiosity and skills mean they may challenge decisions, propose alternatives, or require additional technical validation, which is valuable but labor-intensive."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **opportunity cost**: this kind of partnership can slow down efficiency since the workflow becomes a conversation, not a straightforward execution pipeline. the “cost” of their time needs to be balanced with yours."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**playbook/workflow for highly collaborative clients**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**1. define boundaries upfront**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-9",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**clarify roles**: during onboarding, define what the client’s involvement will look like. is their input advisory? decision-making? are they reviewing drafts or co-creating deliverables?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-10",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**set expectations**: ensure they understand how their input affects timelines. for instance: “when client approvals or revisions exceed 48 hours, deadlines may shift proportionally.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-11",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**decide pricing model**: this type of collaboration could warrant a premium retainer fee or an hourly add-on for meetings, consultations, and decision-making cycles."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**2. design a flexible, transparent workflow**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-14",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**weekly alignment calls**: schedule standing check-ins to discuss progress, gather feedback, and plan adjustments. this keeps feedback structured rather than ad hoc."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-15",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**feedback loops**: build intentional pauses into the workflow where the client’s input is expected, e.g., “we’ll pause for review after phase 1 mockups before proceeding to development.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-16",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**live co-creation sessions**: if the client is technical and prefers deep involvement, consider scheduled Figma/Linear/Slack sessions where you solve problems together in real time."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**3. create a \"decision fatigue\" buffer**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-19",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**pre-digest complex options**: instead of presenting the client with raw decisions, give them a small number of well-reasoned choices to reduce their mental load."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-20",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**agree on decision rules**: for instance, you might agree that minor design tweaks are at your discretion while major UX changes need their review."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**4. leverage tools for collaborative efficiency**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-23",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**task clarity**: for technical clients, use tools like Linear or GitHub to break tasks into small, clear chunks with technical context."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-24",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**versioning**: ensure every change is well-documented (e.g., in GitBook), so the client feels confident in the process without micromanaging."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-25",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**sandbox environments**: provide staging areas or design sandboxes where they can preview work without risking production environments."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**5. adjust timelines & priorities dynamically**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "bulletList",
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "b-28",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**task triage**: give the client visibility into how their requests affect timelines. tools like Notion or Linear with progress bars can be valuable here."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b-29",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "**sprints with flexibility**: define milestones loosely enough to accommodate their input but tightly enough to maintain momentum."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**6. pricing considerations**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "a collaborative, technical client isn’t “just” paying for your execution—they’re paying for your adaptability, facilitation skills, and the ability to integrate their expertise into the final product. that comes at a premium."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. **base retainer + collaboration premium**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- set a higher monthly fee for clients who want active involvement, reflecting the added intensity of the relationship."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- example: a baseline retainer might be $XX,XXX, while a collaborative premium adds $X,XXX for the additional time, meetings, and decision-making cycles."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. **hybrid pricing**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- offer a dual model where standard tasks are covered under the base retainer, but collaboration-intensive work (e.g., co-creation sessions or technical consulting) is billed hourly or at a higher task rate."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. **time-for-money equation**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "- highlight how their time/skills reduce *your* workload (e.g., they already have technical clarity), but balance that by pricing for the increased communication overhead."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**final thought**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "clients like this are high-touch and rewarding, but they require a tailored approach that respects both their contributions and your bandwidth. by building a playbook that formalizes these dynamics, you set the relationship up for mutual success—and ensure you’re compensated fairly for the added layers of complexity. just make sure this is all crystal clear before kickoff. over-communicating upfront will save you down the road."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}